# What must never enter the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and until this file existed that copied the
# whole working tree: the operator's .env with broker keys and SECRET_KEY, the
# live SQLite journals, and the entire .git history. The CI pipeline has a
# DockerHub push path, so anything in the image can leave the machine.

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env is created on the deploy host, so it is present exactly when it is most
# dangerous. Coolify injects environment variables directly and needs no file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/
config/run_config.json
config/run_local.json

# --- Live state ------------------------------------------------------------
# Journals belong in a mounted volume, never baked into an image. A copied
# journal would also be restored on every redeploy, silently resurrecting old
# orders for reconciliation.
data/
logs/
reports/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite3

# --- Version control and CI -------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.dockerignore

# --- Build and cache artefacts ---------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
.next/

# --- Not needed at runtime --------------------------------------------------
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
